From: Local build <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] FIX wayland backend: wl_output follows the refresh rate learned from presentation feedback

WaylandOutput::framePresented takes the host's refresh rate from the presentation feedback and puts it
in the output's mode (setState), but the logical output, which wl_output reports to clients, only
copies its backend output's mode in Workspace::updateOutputs(), on OutputBackend::outputsQueried. The
backend's other mode changes (a host resize, a scale change) emit it; this one did not. So clients
kept the rate the nested output started at for the whole session, while the output device
(kscreen-doctor) showed the real one: 60 Hz upstream, or with 0034 the highest rate among the host's
outputs. On a host with a 5K 165 Hz and a 4K 240 Hz monitor, a guest full screen on the 165 Hz one
told its clients 240 Hz; mpv's --video-sync=display-resample then held 60 fps frames 4 refreshes
(48 images a second, 34 % on cadence) while measuring 164 Hz itself, and Qt Quick's vsync animation
driver advanced by 4.2 ms per 6.1 ms frame. The refresh change now emits outputsQueried like the
others (2026-10-18, findings/two-monitors-brief-2026-10-17.md).
---

diff --git a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
index 6bc612a..253c900 100644
--- a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
@@ -486,6 +486,9 @@ void WaylandOutput::framePresented(struct wp_presentation_feedback *feedback, st
         next.currentMode = mode;
         setState(next);
         m_renderLoop->setRefreshRate(m_refreshRate);
+        // the logical output, and with it wl_output, follows only through the workspace's output
+        // update: without it clients kept the rate the output started at (60 Hz, or the guess)
+        Q_EMIT m_backend->outputsQueried();
     }
     const auto &frame = m_frames.front();
